precept PaymentMethod

# A stateless data-only precept governing a single stored payment method.
# A payment method holds the verified card details and the lightweight
# cardholder-controlled flags (nickname, default selection). The card data
# itself is immutable once stored — re-storing requires creating a new record.
#
# Editability is deliberately minimal: the verified payment instrument fields
# (LastFour, ExpiryMonth, ExpiryYear, CardholderName, CardBrand) are locked at
# storage. Only IsDefault and Nickname can be updated after the card is saved,
# because those are display-layer preferences, not authorization data.

field CardholderName as string optional maxlength 200
field LastFour as string optional maxlength 4
field CardBrand as choice of string("Visa","Mastercard","Amex","Discover","JCB","UnionPay","Other") default "Other"
field ExpiryMonth as integer default 1 min 1 max 12
field ExpiryYear as integer default 2025 min 2025 max 2099

field IsDefault as boolean default false writable
field Nickname as string optional maxlength 50 writable

rule LastFour.length == 4 when LastFour is set because "LastFour {LastFour} must be exactly four digits — the field stores the last four characters of the PAN as a display string"
